    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 6,
        "sourceEnd": 226,
        "text": "Welcome to The School Podcast. Today we're talking about how we report what we hear. I'm your host, Alex, and with me are two students, Mei and Tom. Mei, you've been looking at how students share news. What did you find?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "b50781a7a65ca724aa2cbcb760e8dee910f4acf1d5ab9a8bded2b33e0428e028",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 232,
        "sourceEnd": 465,
        "text": "Well, I interviewed some students—about twenty—and most of them said they get news from social media. But only a few check the source before sharing. One student told me, 'I just share what my friends post.' That's a common attitude.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "bdecd41f14baedded25dde2a7a65c2ea58b40633bcbfdd1e0aa9b108da2639a0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 471,
        "sourceEnd": 735,
        "text": "I read a report that claimed all teenagers trust online news. But I think that's an overgeneralization. The report said most teenagers use social media for news, but it didn't say they all trust it. In fact, some students in my class said they doubt what they see.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "b9eaee25636b77c19654e17d504a4559dcc7460f78840876ab3441d475290e19",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 742,
        "sourceEnd": 782,
        "text": "So you're saying the report exaggerated?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "587740fde33db61c1e1327f5505c0307ac05b6f533c8c32d6b9dd2558beb81bd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 788,
        "sourceEnd": 949,
        "text": "Yes, the writer used 'all' when the evidence only supported 'most'. That's a problem with some media reports—they use strong determiners without enough evidence.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "7cb7eab1906e7d8c61d67dd7c8279e163dcb2e2896919a8211d6b5aa757e0047",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 955,
        "sourceEnd": 1109,
        "text": "Exactly. In my interviews, several students mentioned they check the comments to see if others believe the story. But that's not reliable evidence either.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "ccc6c205d81517bf358bc7ed259e40048472ea883643f9a3c690fa89db9adda8",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1116,
        "sourceEnd": 1148,
        "text": "What about the school newspaper?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "7829a5376d7843afa1fd718e8c7e1b65d7d2d317371e082ec748544450bf9fbb",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "tom",
        "speaker": "Tom",
        "sourceStart": 1154,
        "sourceEnd": 1325,
        "text": "The school newspaper editor told me they verify facts before publishing. She said, 'We require two sources for every story.' But that's the school paper, not social media.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "9062280f3ab88884a5c88f5a9175d8df9e6bc0a68c8101fe56b875038928f627",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mei",
        "speaker": "Mei",
        "sourceStart": 1331,
        "sourceEnd": 1512,
        "text": "Right. So the lesson is: be careful with words like 'all' and 'most'. And when you report what someone said, use verbs like 'claimed', 'stated', or 'admitted' to show your attitude.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "a9f1a1c5413ae9036724541e0548051fe7cc4ec4fec6ce86563892b7c9594d42",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "host",
        "speaker": "Host",
        "sourceStart": 1519,
        "sourceEnd": 1664,
        "text": "Good point. So to summarize, most students get news from social media, some check sources, and not all trust what they see. Thanks for listening.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "cab521ddfc0aa8e3575d1e2c6220a55ae91f795631e6129a6b2d4b2eeb3bea78",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
